      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JASON ROSE (1) was unwanted in betting when starting from the same box but ran very well, finishing in the minors over 395m at Murray Bridge in a Grade 6 in 23.06. Deserves another chance. TIME OF DESIGN (4) was checked in the run and safely held when fifth (19.97) in a OPEN over 342m at Angle Park. Rates a key player and gets chance to atone. ZIPPING NORRIS (8) had a tricky draw last time and although midfield in fourth wasn't far away finishing 3.5 lengths from the winner (20.16). Has never been out of the placings from two starts out of this box. Leading chance. LEFEVRE RICO (2) was a surprise last-start placegetter with solid claims again.",
